  "id": "wolfhirschhorn-syndrome",
  "term": "Wolf–Hirschhorn syndrome",
  "definition": "Wolf–Hirschhorn syndrome is a genetic disorder caused by a large deletion at the end of the short arm of chromosome 4. It commonly involves intellectual disability and developmental delay, along with seizures and a characteristic facial appearance, and may also include midline, heart, and skeletal abnormalities.",
